-- Native Japanese registry from the ASCII surface (s50): the kanji nouns ARE the columns — no ja aliases exist to consult. The unspaced selection is the maximal-munch witness: 北&両手>60 lexes NAME AMP NAME GT NUM. (was s50-native-registry)
-- The s50-s56 suite exercises a registry whose columns, sigils, and system-role names are kanji rather than aliases.
-- The emitter mangles the kanji names to stable BQN identifiers (jp0..); the pins assert through the same mangled columns.
--! registry ../registries/095-native-registry.reg
--! expect 金 = 1100 200 300 1400 500 600

北&両手>60 , 金 += 1000
